{
  "paraphrased_article": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, known for her unconventional life, including claiming clairvoyance and running a healing school, married Durek Verrett, a self-proclaimed shaman from California, in a unique royal wedding. The event in Geiranger, though not a typical royal affair, drew spectators hoping to see the bride. The 52-year-old princess, fourth in line to the Norwegian throne and daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, wed Verrett, 49, in a Church of Norway ceremony at the Hotel Union. Her daughters from her previous marriage, Leah and Emma Behn, served as bridesmaids, alongside a guest list that included various European royals like her brother Crown Prince Haakon and his wife, as well as Crown Princess Victoria of Sweden and Prince Constantijn of the Netherlands, and celebrities like Gwyneth Paltrow. Princess Märtha Louise stepped down from official royal duties in 2022 to separate her and Verrett's business ventures from the Norwegian royal house; Verrett describes himself as an 'energy activator' and 'servant of God'."
}
```

